            %p
          %p
          #SimplicialClassifyingSpaceOfAnOrdinaryGroup.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (simplicial classifying space of an ordinary group)
              %br/
              In the special case that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Groups
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi const
                    %mi SimplicialGroups
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G \in Groups \overset{const}{\hookrightarrow} SimplicialGroups
            %p
              is an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
              regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              (which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WGInComponents"}
              reduce as follows:
            %p
              The simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G
              is that whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p underlying sets are
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi G
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
